      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Capacity, and how the tree divides it. Cohort rows are absent from the tenant panels on purpose: a cohort's nominal contains its children's, so a sum over both would double-count. What is still missing:\n\n| Gap | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Where a tenant's share landed across members | `status.budgets[].perCluster` carries it; no metric exports it yet. |\n| Whether the accounting matches the hardware | Kueue's admitted figure and a pod-derived count are independent views of the same accelerators; nothing compares them. |\n| Tree structure \u2014 parent, depth, violations by reason | The path label lands with the next quota-manager rollout, and until then a tenant band is labelled with its bare name. The rest has no metric, so a rollup still cannot be shown complete rather than assumed. |\n\nNothing here can page anyone: no PrometheusRule is deployed on any cluster and Alertmanager has no receiver.\n\n*The `cluster` picker lists workload clusters only. A management plane holds the authored fleet tree and has no local silicon, so every panel here would be empty for one.*"
